{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_129", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/research_history/profile_episode5.py <<'PY'\nimport importlib.util,time,sys,cProfile,pstats\nimport numpy as np\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('episode5_profile',sys.argv[1]);mod=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\nz=np.load('/workspace/environment/public_assets/dev/seed_303_gaussian_016.npz');args=(z['x'],z['y'],z['r'],z['ry'],int(z['seed']))\np=cProfile.Profile();t=time.perf_counter();p.enable();v=mod.value(*args);p.disable()\nprint('Diagnostic method seconds',time.perf_counter()-t,'shape',v.shape,'finite',np.isfinite(v).all(),'mean',v.mean(),'std',v.std())\npstats.Stats(p).strip_dirs().sort_stats('cumtime').print_stats(40)\nPY\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib\nroot=Path('/tmp/research_history')\nreports=[]\nfor p in sorted(root.glob('*/result.json')):\n if not p.parent.name[:3].isdigit() or int(p.parent.name[:3])<172:continue\n z=json.loads(p.read_text());q=[v for c in z['cases'] for v in c['quality']]\n reports.append({'variant':p.parent.name,'raw_metric':z['raw_metric'],'score':z['score'],'quality_valid':z['quality_valid'],'method_sha256':z['method_sha256'],'worst_nrmse':max(v['normalized_rmse'] for v in q),'min_rho':min(v['spearman'] for v in q),'min_top':min(v['top_quartile_overlap'] for v in q)})\n(root/'episode5_official_summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(reports,indent=2))\nprint('Preserved official summaries',len(reports))\nnotes=Path('/tmp/research_notes.md');notes.write_text('''# Episode 5 in progress\n\nThe best fully evaluated source is **241_numpy_label_take**, raw **0.049951216733218944 seconds**, score **0.9042152790990676**, all 30 cases valid. Exact evaluator hash: **d26af51d56550306674075a9be4114694acf97d6f835602aebeaa9139587b25b**. Worst nRMSE0.0041273241, minimum Spearman0.9999846778, minimum top overlap0.996. Its source and unchanged original report are in \"'`/tmp/research_history/241_numpy_label_take`.\n\nCurrent method.py is temporarily **265_mean_skip3_linear_column** for a complete official evaluation (session84104). Restore241 if slower or invalid.265 combines analytical class initialization, skips one further coarse point update, takes label costs with NumPy, and linearizes the second coupling column factor. All30 local screens pass, worst nRMSE0.0078892385; fresh median0.0400741 vs2410.0441859. Also evaluate264_mean_hard16_linear_column, which had fresh median0.0413984 and worst local nRMSE0.0035865222, before final selection. No concurrent numerical work during official runs.\n\nAll94 episode source snapshots172-265 are preserved.93 have complete local screens,78 pass all30; failures are preserved too. Four official reports complete so far:172 repeated162,190 fused direct arithmetic,224 mean point initialization,241 label take. Five fresh benchmark rounds and all screening logs are saved. `/tmp/research_history/episode_5_working_notes.md` records chronology; `/tmp/research_history/episode_5_index.json` needs updating after final official results. `/tmp/research_history/finalize_episode5.py` selects the best actual valid official report, verifies exact source hash and launcher, restores source, and updates the machine-readable index/selection.\n\nThe frozen solve.sh hash remains **bca6ef61c3a1bc0ded2aa6b2da4734b62072846def679d12a2d7ae669fc88bd1**. Run `sh ./solve.sh`. Only method.py is editable as submission. Starting source162 was repeated officially at0.05629953476842881 with identical source hashf57def419ac069782eeb981cefb9157e8d2a80d927c6794c0cd116203a4b37a6, showing drift relative to previous episode0.0648742. Retain by actual official raw and quality, not local screens.\n\nCompleted work: class grouping preserves outputs but dispatch overhead offsets savings; point/class low precision is mostly slower (broad bfloat point kernels also inaccurate); early mean/moment point initialization works, later polynomial transforms fail unless cubic and expensive; two or three final class updates can be omitted but four fail; simple class subsampling fails badly even with mean correction; deterministic weighted64/80 barycenters pass but fresh speed is worse; vectorized/NumPy clustering reduces their setup cost; direct scale fusion removes dense passes; NumPy np.take is the main measured improvement by avoiding two-dimensional Torch advanced indexing. Cumulative mean initial potentials and last unused candidate transform removals are promising. Full empirical class supports remain in retained241.\n\nPrior history is preserved at `/tmp/research_history/episode_4_continuing_notes.md` and earlier episode notes. No protected targets, private material, evaluator source, credentials, environment variables, network, or other trajectories accessed. No subagents used.\n'\"''')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
